1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,600
Welcome back, today we will build a
simple monthly budget

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:06,700
A budget is just a plan for where
your money goes

3
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,800
First, write down what you earn each
month after tax

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,900
Next, list your fixed costs like
rent, bills, and food

5
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:16,000
Then list the flexible costs like
travel and eating out

6
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:19,100
Subtract the costs from your income
to see what is left

7
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:22,200
If nothing is left, you need to cut
one flexible cost

8
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:25,300
Pick the easiest cut first, small
wins keep you going

9
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:28,400
Put the money you save into a
separate savings account

10
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:29,999
Aim to save ten percent, even five
percent is a good start

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:30,999
A weekly check takes ten minutes and
stops big surprises

12
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,200
Check your spending once a week, not
once a month

13
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:37,300
Use cash for food if card spending
always runs over

14
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:40,400
Keep one fun budget, cutting
everything never lasts

15
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:43,500
At the end of the month, compare the
plan with the real numbers

16
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:46,600
Move any leftover money to savings on
the first of the month

17
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:49,700
Next lesson we will look at paying
off a small debt

18
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:52,800
Thanks for learning with me, try the
budget this week

